[67.057913, "o", "\u001b[2m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[67.05824, "o", "\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[36mResults\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[32m9 passed\u001b[0m, \u001b[31m0 failed\u001b[0m, 9 total\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[36mSummary — Anthropic vs AWS Bedrock\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  The same Claude Sonnet 4 model is served by \u001b[1mtwo cloud providers\u001b[0m.\r\n  Provider-specific auth (header, prefix, path) is driven by \u001b[1mprovider_profiles\u001b[0m.\r\n  API keys come from \u001b[1mAuthorino\u001b[0m (K8s Secrets → header injection).\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mWhat the error messages prove:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n    \u001b[1mTest\u001b[0m  \u001b[1mError from\u001b[0m   \u001b[1mError message proves\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m────  ──────────  ─────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n    1     Anthropic    \"invalid x-api-key\" → correct auth header\r\n    2     Bedrock      \"security token invalid\" → correct Bearer format\r\n    3     Anthropic    reached preferred provider (not Bedrock fallback)\r\n    4     Anthropic    Bob's key (different from Alice's in test 1)\r\n    5     Bedrock      Carol's key reached Bedrock\r\n    6     Router       200 + \"no credential\" → fail-closed, no fallback\r\n    7     Router       200 + \"no credential\" → fail-closed, no fallback"]
[67.058285, "o", "\r\n    8-9   Authorino    401 → request never reached router/provider\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mKey files:\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mRouter config:  scripts/demo-multi-provider/anthropic-bedrock/config.yaml\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mEnvoy config:   scripts/demo-multi-provider/anthropic-bedrock/envoy.yaml\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[67.058313, "o", "    \u001b[2mAuthConfig:     scripts/demo-multi-provider/anthropic-bedrock/k8s-authconfig.yaml\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mSecrets:        scripts/demo-multi-provider/anthropic-bedrock/k8s-secrets.yaml\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[67.058404, "o", "\u001b[2m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
